how to batch in boost together  in this video we'll see how to batch  input sequences together  in general the sentences we want to pass  through our model  we want to allow the same length here we  are using the model we saw  in the sentiment analysis pipeline and  want to classify  two sentences when tokenizing them and  mapping each token to its corresponding  input ids  we get two lists of different lengths  trying to create a tensor on a bi array  from those two lists  will result in an error because all  arrays and 10 source  should be rectangular one way to  overcome this limit is to make the  second sentence the same length as the  first  by adding a special token as many times  as necessary  another way would be to truncate the  first sequence to the length of the  second  but we would then lose a lot of  information that may be necessary to  properly classify the sentence  in general we only truncate sentences  when they are longer than the maximum  length the model can handle  the value used to pass the second  sentence should not be picked randomly  the model has been pre-trained with a  certain padding id which you can find  in tokenizer.pad tokenity  now that we have padded our sentences we  can make a batch with them  if we pass the two sentences to the  models separately or patched together  however  we notice that we don't get the same  results for the sentence that is padded  here the second one is that the bug in  the transformers library  no if you remember that transformer  models make av use of attention layers  this should not come as a total surprise  when computing the contextual  representation of each token  the attention layers look at all the  other words in the sentence  if we have just the sentence or the  sentence with several padding tokens  added  is surgical we don't get the same values  to get the same results with or without  padding we need to indicate to the  attention layers  that we should ignore the spanning  tokens this is done by creating an  attention  mask a tensor with the same shape as the  input ids  with zeros and ones once  indicate the tokens the attention layers  should consider in the context  and zeroes the tokens we should ignore  now passing this attention mask along  with input ids  will give us the same results as when we  send the two sentences individually to  the model  this is all done behind the scenes by  the tokenizer when you apply it to  several sentences with the flag  padding equal to it will apply the  padding with a proper value to the  smaller sentences  and create the appropriate attention  mask
 

